-- so re-running the script is a no-op instead of a silent partial write.
INSERT INTO imported_classes (class_id, name, system, markdown, status, created_by)
SELECT 'hu-bionics', 'Bionics', 'heroes-unlimited', '---
id: hu-bionics
name: Bionics
system: heroes-unlimited
source_book: Revised Heroes Unlimited p.60-68
category: rcc
hit_points_base: "P.E. + 1D6 per level"
sdc_base: "30"
starting_money: "4d4x100"
special_abilities:
  - name: "Bionic Reconstruction Budget"
    description: "Printed 60. A construction budget rolled on a percentile table - 01-17 $6.6 million, 18-33 $7.2, 34-49 $8, 50-66 $8.5, 67-84 $9, 85-00 $9.5 million - spent entirely on bionic components and weapons from printed 61-68. ALL of it must be spent; anything left over is permanently lost. It cannot buy automobiles, handguns or anything that is not a bionic component. Much of the horrendous cost is the micronisation, the rarity and the operation that merges machine with man. Buy spare parts: a character who has broken with his creators cannot easily replace what he loses - though a mechanism needing surgery is not a reasonable spare."
  - name: "Condition That Led to Reconstruction"
    description: "Printed 60. 01-20 a healthy specimen, destitute or fantastically motivated toward bionic research and deemed psychologically suitable; 21-40 lost both legs or both arms to disease or accident; 41-60 paraplegic with no hope of recovery; 61-80 a deteriorating bone or muscle disease with no hope of a normal life; 81-00 completely paralysed with no brain damage and no hope of recovery."
restrictions: ["Bionic budget money buys bionic components and weapons and nothing else - not a car, not a handgun"]
extraction_notes: "THIS IS A CONSTRUCTION SYSTEM AND ONLY ITS FRAME IS IMPORTED. A bionic character IS his components: printed 61-68 price major body parts, ear and eye special features, optics and sensors, eye and hand weapons, retractable blades, lungs, mouth and throat features, exoskeletons and bionic body armour, and the player spends six to nine million dollars across them. The catalog has no builder and `gear` holds one `mdc`, one `damage`, one `range` - the same argument that kept the robot and super-vehicle systems out and Phase World''s vessels before them. Survey D7, BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT F3. What ships is the class: the base S.D.C., the personal money, the standard education, and the two tables as prose. A TYPICAL BIONIC LIMB HAS 30 S.D.C. OF ITS OWN, separate from the character''s 30, and there is no field for a per-limb pool. STARTING_MONEY IS THE PERSONAL CASH, NOT THE BUDGET: 4D4x100 dollars, which is the money the character actually carries. The budget is millions and is spent before play begins."
---

## Lore

The bionic character is a human being rebuilt with machinery. The creation of
one is a little more complex than most of the other power categories, because
the player actually builds the character: a budget is rolled, and then the
abilities, sensors, weapons and gimmicks that compose the cyborg are bought one
at a time. Note paper and a calculator help.

Low physical attributes do not matter here. They are likely to change with the
addition of bionics.

Even a cyborg is still human. The base S.D.C. is the same 30 anyone else has,
and it grows through physical training; exoskeletons and bionic body armour are
artificial means of adding more protection on top.

## GM Notes

**The bionic budget**, printed 60 - all of it must be spent:

| roll | budget | roll | budget |
|---|---|---|---|
| 01-17 | $6.6 million | 50-66 | $8.5 million |
| 18-33 | $7.2 million | 67-84 | $9 million |
| 34-49 | $8 million | 85-00 | $9.5 million |

Decide first which body parts are being replaced, then buy the most important
and basic items, then the gimmicks. A character may be made as human or as
mechanical in appearance as taste dictates.

**The sponsoring organization**, printed 60: 01-25 a medical research facility;
26-50 private industry; 51-75 a secret organization - roll again for its motive,
01-20 medical, 21-50 criminal, 51-80 crime fighting, 81-00 military; 76-00 the
military.

**Standing with it**, printed 60-61: 01-19 allowed to leave on very good terms;
20-41 allowed to leave after great antagonism, not friendly but may still help;
42-64 thrown out of the program, all ties permanently dissolved and very hostile;
65-89 ran away and secretly hunted, hostile but not necessarily deadly; 90-00 ran
away and considered a criminal or extremely dangerous, hunted by law enforcement
and by the organization.

Hand to hand combat is not automatic and must be selected as a learned skill.
Every hero gets two attacks per melee; more come from hand to hand and boxing.
Other than what is built into the cyborg, only conventional weaponry and
equipment are available - unless the character is employed by the organization
that built him or on good terms with it, in which case all types of facilities
and equipment may be open to him. A typical bionic limb has an S.D.C. of 30 of
its own.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-bionics');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-bionics';

